(6504709, 966099, 60614, '<td valign="top">Wow, this is awesome.  I love the POV and your processing is to die for.  Well done.</td>', 'Wow, this is awesome.  I love the POV and your processing is to die for.  Well done.', '2011-08-15 09:36:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(6504710, 966111, 114233, '<td valign="top">A lovely moody image and certainly deserves the high placing. I agree with <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_N.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_N.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_N.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=96751" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">tanguera</a> that the grass in the FG could have been burned a bit too keep the focus on the house a bit more. Excellent use of a long exposure together with the PP. I find it interesting that some of the grass in front of you didnt move that much in the 25 sec exposure - judging by the angle some of the grass is bending over at, I wonder if it wasnt your body forming a bit of a wind break?</td>', 'A lovely moody image and certainly deserves the high placing. I agree with  tanguera that the grass in the FG could have been burned a bit too keep the focus on the house a bit more. Excellent use of a long exposure together with the PP. I find it interesting that some of the grass in front of you didnt move that much in the 25 sec exposure - judging by the angle some of the grass is bending over at, I wonder if it wasnt your body forming a bit of a wind break?', '2011-08-15 09:37:12.000000', NULL, 0),
